{
  "name": "cloud-itonami-isic-0111",
  "main": "dist/worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-30",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "observability": { "enabled": true }
  // Deployed into the ai-gftd-repository-dispatch namespace (Workers for
  // Platforms), not as a standalone Worker:
  //
  //     wrangler deploy --dispatch-namespace ai-gftd-repository-dispatch
  //
  // That is what makes the fleet's scale possible. There are ~1,200 actors
  // and a Worker each would run past the ordinary per-account script cap;
  // user Workers in a dispatch namespace are not bound by it, which is the
  // product's whole purpose. It also matches what these actors ARE: they
  // wake for a request and stop, so none of them wants a route of its own.
  //
  // NO D1 binding. Storage is kotobase.net through
  // kotoba-lang/kotobase-client, so authorization, tenant isolation and
  // replay protection are the service's rather than this Worker's.
  //
  // Secrets (`wrangler secret put`), never placed here:
  //   KOTOBASE_SECRET_KEY  this actor's own Ed25519 seed (base64, 32 bytes).
  //                        The client mints a CACAO per request from it; the
  //                        key-derived graph IS this actor's namespace.
  //   CEREALOPS_WRITE_TOKEN gates POST /operations. Reads are open.
}
